2938 0 obj
<</A 2939 0 R/Alt(Graph showing Tyson Foods" materiality assessment across three key categories: environmental, social, and governance/other. The horizontal axis represents "Importance to Business", and the vertical axis represents "Importance to Stakeholders." The graph is divided into three vertical sections. In the first section, the key issues within the governance category, with respect to stakeholders, are "Corporate Governance", followed by "Political Engagement & Lobbying Practices" with respect to business". In the second section, the environmental key issues include "Water Stewardship", "Land Stewardship", "Waste Reduction, Recycling & Reuse", and "Sustainable Packaging"; the social key issues include "Human Rights & Labor Relations", "Affordability & Access", "Diversity Equity & Inclusion", and "Community Investment & Economic Impact"; and the Governance/Other key issues include "Business Ethics & Anti-Corruption", "Alternative Proteins & Product Innovation", and "Data Privacy & Cybersecurity. In the third section \(most important\), the environmental key issues include "Climate Change & GHG emissions" and "Animal Health & Welfare"; the social key issues include "Team Member Health & Safety", "Team Member Wellbeing & Engagement", and "Talent Attraction, Development & Retention"; and the Governance/Other key issues include "Product Safety, Quality & Responsibility" and "Supply Chain Management & Traceability.␀)/K 68/P 2623 0 R/Pg 424 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
